msgid "Common fixes for poor video quality"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-cameras-and-gimbals.rst:79
#: b90a2fc91b184a95a027f0eac8faf52f
msgid "Some of the more common causes and solutions for poor video are listed below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-cameras-and-gimbals.rst:82
#: 0d3c9770c94d46b58acaecef57aa8a8c
msgid "\"Jello\" effect (or rolling shutter) is a by-product of using a camera with a CMOS sensor (GoPro, et al) caused by vibration from unbalanced props/motors and can be mitigated by mounting the camera on soft rubber, silicone, foam ear plugs or sometimes just on velcro."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-cameras-and-gimbals.rst:86
#: b99f1c2291bf42369ba076db5f547ad4
msgid "digital and optical stabilization systems found in many cameras often do not perform well because of the vibrations found on many multicopters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-cameras-and-gimbals.rst:90
#: 141c498c66374fd09e91872c63b34907
msgid "Exceptions: the Sony video camera balanced steady shot system is very effective even at maximum 30 power zoom."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-cameras-and-gimbals.rst:93
#: 823b3cbce4e746c7a32b53b819f213d3
msgid "For better and smoother Yaw, use Expo control on your RC and lower the :ref:`ACRO_Y_RATE<ACRO_Y_RATE>` gain in the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-cameras-and-gimbals.rst:96
#: 4613859199894190940d309ce47323ea
msgid "It is important to remember that even with a perfect setup, photography is an art as well as a science. Using the camera pointing straight to the ground is a good place to start, but more dramatic viewpoints can be achieved with angles other than vertical. Mount about 40 degrees deviation from vertical to obtain mainly ground photos but with an oblique view. About 70 degrees off vertical will give you a lot more sky thus giving more scenic photos. ArduPilot will stabilize the gimbal to whatever position you set."
msgstr ""
